body:
The logic for checking form label association is incomplete. The presence of an `id` attribute on an input doesn't guarantee it's properly labeled - there must be a corresponding `<label for="id">` element or the input must be wrapped in a label. This check will miss form inputs that have an ID but no associated label element, creating false negatives in accessibility testing.
```suggestion
    const id = element.getAttribute('id');
    const doc = element.ownerDocument || document;
    const hasAssociatedLabel =
      !!element.closest('label') ||
      (!!id && !!doc.querySelector(`label[for="${id}"]`));
    const hasLabel = hasAriaLabel || hasAssociatedLabel;
```
